      "content": "mators.\nVI. CONCLUSION\nWe presented CoHyFuse, a condition-aware ROI-centered\nhypergraph fusion framework for task-fMRI prediction. CoHy-\nFuse constructs condition-wise top-Kq hypergraphs and fuses\nHGNN-based condition embeddings with a complementary\nwhole-session FC branch. Experiments on AABC and CMI-\nHBN benchmarks showed the best mean performance among\nevaluated baselines, and ablations supported the contributions\nof condition-specific hypergraph construction, heterogeneous\nKq, and dual-branch fusion. Interpretability analysis further\nidentified DIST-related SAN–FPN and SAN–SAN motifs as\nmodel-relevant patterns associated with FCC. Overall, Co-\nHyFuse provides a compact and interpretable framework for\nmodeling state-resolved hypergraph-defined ROI-set structure\nin task-fMRI.\nREFERENCES"
