      "content": "behaviorally relevant individual differences and that task-\nstate FC carries functional information beyond resting-state\nconnectivity [1]. The operator-control and Kq analyses fur-\nther support modeling task-fMRI beyond pairwise ROI–ROI\ngraphs: replacing HGNN with GCN/GAT variants reduced\nperformance, and condition-specific hypergraph construction\nwas more effective than a shared neighborhood scale. This is\nconsistent with prior hypergraph connectomics evidence that\nmulti-ROI topological patterns can carry task- and behavior-\nrelevant information [6]. In CoHyFuse, the condition-wise hy-\npergraph branch captures state-dependent FC-profile neighbor-\nhood structure, whereas the whole-session FC branch provides\na compact summary of session-level connectivity."
